        <GrantAmt>2894</GrantAmt>
        <Desc>GENERAL PROGRAMS: GENERAL PROGRAMS INCLUDED ACTIVITIES RANGING FROM THOUGHT LEADERSHIP PAPERS AND REACH ON A VARIETY OF TOPICS IN HEALTHCARE INCLUDING APPLICATION OF AI IN HELATHCARE, CHAPTER SUBMISSIONS TO BOOKS, ARTICLES ON EQUITY, SOCIAL DETERMINANTS OF HEALTH, ETC.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>42900</ExpenseAmt>
        <Desc>PROVIDE ENHANCED CARE MANAGEMENT (ECM) BIRTH EQUITY SERVICES FOCUSED ON SUPPORTING PREGNANT AND POSTPARTUM INDIVIDUALS WHO FACE ELEVATED SOCIAL AND MEDICAL RISKS. THROUGH CULTURALLY ALIGNED, COMMUNITY-BASED CARE COORDINATION AND DOULA SUPPORT, REACH HEALTHCARE ADDRESSES DISPARITIES IN MATERNAL AND INFANT HEALTH OUTCOMES BY IMPROVING ACCESS TO PREVENTIVE CARE, REDUCING AVOIDABLE HOSPITALIZATIONS, AND PROMOTING HEALTHIER PREGNANCIESAND BIRTHS. IN 2024 WE LAUNCHED THIS SERVICE LINE; CONTRACTED WITH ONE MAJOR MANAGED CARE ORGANIZATION FOR DELIVERING SERVICES; AND HIRED AND TRAINED STAFF.</Desc>
